{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-10-19T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"If parks could keep birthday diaries, Eryri National Park (Snowdonia) in Wales would have quite the story to tell. The park turns 75 today, marking the anniversary of its designation in 1951. Eryri stretches across 2,130 square kilometres, with nine mountain ranges, 119 kilometres of coastline and habitats ranging from peatlands and native woodlands to upland landscapes. At more than 1,050 metres, Yr Wyddfa is Eryri's highest point. Nearby, the Carneddau and Glyderau add their own peaks, while Cadair Idris rises in the south. These protected landscapes provide habitats for wildlife and include 17 National Nature Reserves and 56 Sites of Special Scientific Interest.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.DolbadarnWales_ROW9422076532_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.DolbadarnWales_ROW9422076532_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Dolbadarn Castle, Llanberis, Eryri National Park (Snowdonia), Wales","Copyright":"© joe daniel price/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261018_DolbadarnWales\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Eryri+National+Park+Wales&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261018_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261018_DolbadarnWales"},"Ssd":"20261018","Name":"DolbadarnWales","Market":"ROW","Hash":"9422076532","FullDateString":"18. lokak. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Perugia has a walkway with a story beneath every step: its medieval aqueduct. Construction began in 1254, and by around 1280, the aqueduct was carrying water from Monte Pacciano to the Fontana Maggiore in the city centre. The clever bit? Engineers found a way to make the water flow uphill. Using a pressurised conduit, the system overcame the city's steep terrain—an impressive feat of medieval engineering.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.PerugiaAqueduct_ROW9255897123_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.PerugiaAqueduct_ROW9255897123_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Medieval Aqueduct, Perugia, Italy","Copyright":"© Marco Saracco/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261017_PerugiaAqueduct\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Medieval+Aqueduct+Perugia&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261017_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261017_PerugiaAqueduct"},"Ssd":"20261017","Name":"PerugiaAqueduct","Market":"ROW","Hash":"9255897123","FullDateString":"17. lokak. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Some mountains make you work for the view. Mount Sneffels makes you work for the last few hundred metres. Rising to 4,310 metres in Colorado's San Juan Mountains, this fourteener is a familiar sight around Ridgway, Ouray and Telluride. It sits within the 67-square-kilometre Mount Sneffels Wilderness, a protected area designated in 1980. Hikers can reach the mountain from several approaches, including the Yankee Boy Basin and the Blue Lakes area.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SneffelsAutumn_ROW9027717849_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SneffelsAutumn_ROW9027717849_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Mount Sneffels in the San Juan Mountains near Ridgway, Colorado, United States","Copyright":"© lightphoto/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261016_SneffelsAutumn\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Mount+Sneffels&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261016_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261016_SneffelsAutumn"},"Ssd":"20261016","Name":"SneffelsAutumn","Market":"ROW","Hash":"9027717849","FullDateString":"16. lokak. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"People have been coming to Niagara Falls, on the Canada-US border, for centuries to admire the view. A few, however, decided admiring it from a safe distance was overrated. In 1901, Annie Edson Taylor climbed into a barrel and became the first recorded person to survive going over the Falls. Others followed with their own stunts, although such attempts are now illegal. The Falls have also inspired artists, filmmakers and musicians, with Hollywood giving them a starring role in 'Niagara' (1953), featuring Marilyn Monroe and Joseph Cotten.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.NiagaraOnt_ROW1418204353_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.NiagaraOnt_ROW1418204353_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Horseshoe Falls illuminated at night in Niagara Falls, Ontario, Canada","Copyright":"© Jianmei Wang/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261015_NiagaraOnt\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Horseshoe+Falls+Niagara+Falls&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261015_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261015_NiagaraOnt"},"Ssd":"20261015","Name":"NiagaraOnt","Market":"ROW","Hash":"1418204353","FullDateString":"15. lokak. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"How do we know what Earth looked like long before humans appeared? Fossils provide many clues. Palaeontological discoveries help scientists reconstruct past environments, trace the evolution of life and learn about creatures that vanished millions of years ago. From dinosaurs to tiny marine organisms, these remnants of the past preserve snapshots of ancient worlds that no longer exist.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AmmoniteFossils_ROW1149504413_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AmmoniteFossils_ROW1149504413_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Ammonite fossils from the Jurassic Period","Copyright":"© J Nemchinova/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261014_AmmoniteFossils\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Ammonite+fossils&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261014_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261014_AmmoniteFossils"},"Ssd":"20261014","Name":"AmmoniteFossils","Market":"ROW","Hash":"1149504413","FullDateString":"14. lokak. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Water seems to be everywhere at Plitvice Lakes National Park in Croatia. Sixteen terraced lakes are linked by a network of waterfalls, streams and cascades that wind through forested limestone canyons. The constantly changing colours of the water, ranging from emerald green to deep blue, are shaped by minerals, sunlight and ever-changing reflections. Established in 1949, Plitvice Lakes is Croatia's oldest and largest national park. The landscape is famous for its tufa barriers, natural limestone formations created as mineral-rich water deposits calcium carbonate over centuries. These barriers continue to grow and change, gradually transforming the park's waterfalls and lakes.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.PlitviceAutumn_ROW0890292044_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.PlitviceAutumn_ROW0890292044_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Plitvice Lakes National Park, Croatia","Copyright":"© Jan Wlodarczyk/Alamy","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261013_PlitviceAutumn\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Plitvice+Lakes+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261013_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261013_PlitviceAutumn"},"Ssd":"20261013","Name":"PlitviceAutumn","Market":"ROW","Hash":"0890292044","FullDateString":"13. lokak. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"What do you get when a railway, a lifeboat station and a seaside day out meet at the water's edge? Mumbles Pier. Stretching 255 metres into Swansea Bay, this Victorian landmark opened on 10 May 1898 and has been part of the Welsh coast ever since.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.MumblesSwansea2026_ROW0047867144_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.MumblesSwansea2026_ROW0047867144_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Mumbles Pier, Swansea, Wales","Copyright":"© Helen Hotson/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261012_MumblesSwansea2026\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Mumbles+Pier+Wales&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261012_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261012_MumblesSwansea2026"},"Ssd":"20261012","Name":"MumblesSwansea2026","Market":"ROW","Hash":"0047867144","FullDateString":"12. lokak. 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"When night falls in Jasper National Park, Alberta, Canada, the mountains get a whole new backdrop. Designated a Dark-Sky Preserve in 2011, the park spans more than 11,000 square kilometres, with measures in place to reduce light pollution. Here, the stars, planets and the Milky Way put up a celestial show, giving visitors a reason to look up. Then morning arrives and the focus shifts from the sky above to the landscape below.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.MaligneFest_ROW1322674228_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.MaligneFest_ROW1322674228_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Maligne Lake, Jasper National Park, Alberta, Canada","Copyright":"© Andrey Popov/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261025_MaligneFest\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Jasper+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261025_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261025_MaligneFest"},"Ssd":"20261025","Name":"MaligneFest","Market":"ROW","Hash":"1322674228","FullDateString":"25. lokak. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In much of Brazil, July is synonymous with cold weather, mist and muted tones. The green-headed tanager goes in the opposite direction. Green, blue, turquoise, yellow, black, orange and touches of violet come together on a body just over 13 centimetres long, appearing among the branches like a living argument for extravagance. It is no surprise that it frequently features on lists of the most beautiful birds in the world.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Tanager_ROW0977269473_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Tanager_ROW0977269473_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Green-headed tanager","Copyright":"© Juan Carlos Vindas/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261024_Tanager\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Green-headed+tanager&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261024_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261024_Tanager"},"Ssd":"20261024","Name":"Tanager","Market":"ROW","Hash":"0977269473","FullDateString":"24. lokak. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Two grey wolves move through the sagebrush of Yellowstone National Park in Wyoming, home to some of North America's most closely watched wolf packs. Their thick coats help them withstand harsh winters, and their keen senses make them skilled hunters and communicators.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.YellowstoneWolves_ROW0688697251_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.YellowstoneWolves_ROW0688697251_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Two grey wolves, Yellowstone National Park, Wyoming, United States","Copyright":"© John Morrison/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261023_YellowstoneWolves\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Yellowstone+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261023_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261023_YellowstoneWolves"},"Ssd":"20261023","Name":"YellowstoneWolves","Market":"ROW","Hash":"0688697251","FullDateString":"23. lokak. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Few places in South Korea capture the magic of autumn quite like Naejangsan National Park, where mountainsides glow in brilliant shades of scarlet, orange, yellow and gold. Located in the country's southwest, the park is particularly famous for its vivid maple colours, making it one of Korea's premier destinations for autumn scenery. Its name, meaning 'many secrets in the mountains,' reflects the varied landscapes found throughout the region.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.NaejangsanNP_ROW0481262720_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.NaejangsanNP_ROW0481262720_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Autumn in Naejangsan National Park, South Korea","Copyright":"© Twenty47studio/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261022_NaejangsanNP\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Naejangsan+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261022_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261022_NaejangsanNP"},"Ssd":"20261022","Name":"NaejangsanNP","Market":"ROW","Hash":"0481262720","FullDateString":"22. lokak. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Bridging the gap between old and new, Nguyen Hoang Bridge gives Hue's skyline a fresh connection. Spanning the Perfume River in Vietnam, the modern steel-arch landmark opened to traffic on March 26, 2025. Its design, called 'The Crane Facing Thien Mu,' draws inspiration from a local legend and nearby Thien Mu Pagoda.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.VietnamBridge_ROW0147548772_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.VietnamBridge_ROW0147548772_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Nguyen Hoang Bridge over the Perfume River, Hue, Vietnam","Copyright":"© VU PHAM VAN/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261021_VietnamBridge\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Hue+Vietnam&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261021_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261021_VietnamBridge"},"Ssd":"20261021","Name":"VietnamBridge","Market":"ROW","Hash":"0147548772","FullDateString":"21. lokak. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Slow and steady wins the race—and the brown-throated sloth seems perfectly happy to skip the race altogether. This three-toed mammal has a different approach to life: conserve energy, hang on and take your time.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.BrownSloth_ROW9869731535_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.BrownSloth_ROW9869731535_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Brown-throated sloth, Puerto Viejo de Talamanca, Costa Rica","Copyright":"© Suzi Eszterhas/Minden Pictures","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261020_BrownSloth\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Brown+throated+sloth&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261020_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261020_BrownSloth"},"Ssd":"20261020","Name":"BrownSloth","Market":"ROW","Hash":"9869731535","FullDateString":"20. lokak. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"What if a city's busiest street had no road? In Venice, Italy, traffic flows along the Grand Canal, a 3.8-kilometre waterway that winds through the city in a giant reverse S-shape. Known to locals as the Canalazzo, it is Venice's main water-traffic corridor, carrying vaporetti, water taxis, gondolas, police boats and other vessels. The canal follows the course of an ancient river that once flowed into the Venetian Lagoon.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.VeniceSunrise_ROW9643744702_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.VeniceSunrise_ROW9643744702_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Grand Canal in Venice, Italy","Copyright":"© Juan Romero/Cavan Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261019_VeniceSunrise\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Grand+Canal+Venice&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261019_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261019_VeniceSunrise"},"Ssd":"20261019","Name":"VeniceSunrise","Market":"ROW","Hash":"9643744702","FullDateStr